### Method 1: Iterative Loop (The Standard Approach)

This is the most fundamental and robust way to calculate the length. It iterates through the string character by character until it encounters the null terminator (`\0`).

```c
#include <stdio.h>

/**
 * @brief Calculates the length of a null-terminated string without using strlen().
 * 
 * @param str The string to measure.
 * @return int The length of the string (number of characters before the null terminator).
 */
int custom_strlen(const char *str) {
    if (str == NULL) {
        return 0; // Handle the case where the input pointer is NULL
    }

    int length = 0;
    // Loop until the current character pointed to by 'str' is the null terminator ('\0')
    while (str[length] != '\0') {
        length++;
    }
    return length;
}

